{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews","id":1359863,"title":"Old Gods with Modern Purviews","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-09T01:35:14-08:00","id":1359863,"title":"Old Gods with Modern Purviews","content":"Stated as slight off-topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1359842#post1359842\">here</a>, we entered in to discussion of how classical Pantheons Gods could take modern Purviews \u2013 for example, Internet. Open topic for lists I will compile once in a while from posts. Only rule \u2013 we propose maximum two gods per Pantheon per concept, so do not having every long lists of things.<br /> <br /> Starting list compiled from my and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> propositions:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Internet</b></span><br /> <br /> Aesir - Heimdall?<br /> Theoi \u2013 Hermes, Iris - she's <i>at least</i> as qualified for the role as Hermes is.<br /> Netjar \u2013 Isis<br /> Devas - Sarasvati, Goddess of Arts and Letters.<br /> Kami - Tsukiyomi - he's big on travel and gossip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-09-2020, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T09:26:36-08:00","id":1359909,"title":"","content":"I have this image in my head of Hades and Hermes going into the banking business together during the Renaissance, and this being part of the backstory of Hades's offspring Mammon.<br /> <br /> Also Ares and Heph\u00e6stus arguing over who gets atomic energy during the 40s and 50s, which Aphrodite ends up finding so tiresome that she goes off and helps start the free love hippie subculture as a response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T12:45:16-08:00","id":1359944,"title":"","content":"Did you try reading the corebook? Where many of the entries talk about roles that the Gods take in the modern day? Or miss the point I made in the thread you cited about how you're looking at the internet as a purview all wrong?<br /> <br /> And to copy my contribution from that thread to here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each God would find their niche with the Internet as the medium and draw the lines in that.<br /> <br /> Sarasvati, the Muses, Thoth/Djhuety, other Patrons of Arts and Written Word would claim the written stuff on the internet.<br /> <br /> Loki and Tezcatlipoca would take great delight in trolling subcultures.<br /> <br /> Online dating and matchmaking sites? There are canonically in Scion several Gods that bless them. </div> </div> </div>Other examples of Gods Adapting could include Hephaestus blessing modern factories, Xochipilli being all about dance clubs where ecstasy is handed out like Skittles, Artemis becoming a patron of modern parks and conservation efforts, and the Tuatha de Danann formally accepting Rap Battles as a Noble Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T13:05:55-08:00","id":1359949,"title":"","content":"I cant find it now but i wrote some musing on which gods like which type of video games.<br /> <br /> Only one i remember right now is Odin likes counter strike and other very competitive video games but he always ends up cheating and having his accounts banned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T13:34:49-08:00","id":1359958,"title":"","content":"Ooh found it. <br /> Meh most of it is boring, like Athena liking RTS games.<br /> <br /> But that might be funny.<br /> <br /> It might surprise someone to learn that the Tuatha De Danann love to play Minecraft.<br /> The only thing is that they are just about the worst sort of griefers out there.<br /> It wouldnt be strange for a TDD to come back to their minecraft castle one morning only to find it had been burned and tnted to the ground with a signpost in front reading.<br /> &quot;LOL newb.<br /> Stole all your cows.<br /> Signed Lugh &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T14:54:02-08:00","id":1359972,"title":"","content":"I like to believe that Set, Ares, and Loki all consider outlaw motorcycle gangs as falling under their influence, which is part of what inspired my idea for the Lords of Chaos cult/motorcycle club.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T01:50:17-08:00","id":1361420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews#post1359863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stated as slight off-topic <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1359842#post1359842&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, we entered in to discussion of how classical Pantheons Gods could take modern Purviews \u2013 for example, Internet. Open topic for lists I will compile once in a while from posts. Only rule \u2013 we propose maximum two gods per Pantheon per concept, so do not having every long lists of things.<br /> <br /> Starting list compiled from my and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> propositions:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Internet</b></span><br /> <br /> Aesir - Heimdall?<br /> Theoi \u2013 Hermes, Iris - she's <i>at least</i> as qualified for the role as Hermes is.<br /> Netjar \u2013 Isis<br /> Devas - Sarasvati, Goddess of Arts and Letters.<br /> Kami - Tsukiyomi - he's big on travel and gossip.</div> </div> </div> </div>No way man Internet is definitely Odin, he was also all seeing but he also included all knowing. The I internet is one of his ravens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:52:06-08:00","id":1361483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361420#post1361420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No way man Internet is definitely Odin, he was also all seeing but he also included all knowing. The I internet is one of his ravens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one he uses to contact worthwhile heroes that are not from martial backgrounds (a modern war needs its accountants and scientists, after all)<br /> <br /> Huginn, Muninn, and Linkedinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 01-17-2020, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T10:08:45-08:00","id":1361515,"title":"","content":"Pft. The internet is clearly Athena's purview. Ain't you kids heard of ARPANET.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T10:38:51-08:00","id":1361519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361515#post1361515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pft. The internet is clearly Athena's purview. Ain't you kids heard of ARPANET.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Neal Stephenson, in his novel Cryptonomicon, presenting the idea that Athena is the goddess of technology. Which does fit with the idea that she invented a number of things that make agricultural societies possible, taught mortals mathematics, and was highly skilled at a number of crafts that required technological tools. I could easily see her taking an early interest in computers and programming languages<sup>1</sup>. I could also see Ada Lovelace being one of her Scions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>Also flying machines, automobiles, cameras, the printing press, and a dozen other things. When Demigod comes out, I'm likely going to invent a group of Athenean offspring who are now the minor goddesses of various technologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-17-2020, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T11:05:07-08:00","id":1361522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361519#post1361519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember Neal Stephenson, in his novel Cryptonomicon, presenting the idea that Athena is the goddess of technology. Which does fit with the idea that she invented a number of things that make agricultural societies possible, taught mortals mathematics, and was highly skilled at a number of crafts that required technological tools. I could easily see her taking an early interest in computers and programming languages<sup>1</sup>. I could also see Ada Lovelace being one of her Scions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>Also flying machines, automobiles, cameras, the printing press, and a dozen other things. When Demigod comes out, I'm likely going to invent a group of Athenean offspring who are now the minor goddesses of various technologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense to Stephenson, but if Athena is God of Technology what does that make Hephaestus? You know, the actual Greek God of building things and the like?<br /> <br /> But yes, this kind of overlap is exactly why i said &quot;Having a singular God of the Internet is looking at it the wrong way&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T12:33:50-08:00","id":1361543,"title":"","content":"Also, whoever actually takes the Internet as a purview has ascended to an equivalent of Zeus/Poseidon/Hades in terms of Sky/Sea/Earth. That'd be a fun conversation to have amongst the Theoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T14:01:08-08:00","id":1361564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361522#post1361522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense to Stephenson, but if Athena is God of Technology what does that make Hephaestus? You know, the actual Greek God of building things and the like?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly from a monologue by a character who was, IIRC (and I may be getting my streams crossed with Gregoy Keyes's Age of Unreason), part of a secret society dedicated to Athena, and largely had to do with her being about fighting wars with brains rather than pure brawn. But part of it went into the idea of her being a symbol - or in the case of Scion, an insperation and motivator - for technological development and its applications to warfare, especially the concept of cryptography. He also talks about how while Athena and Ares are both war gods, they are very different incarnations of the subject. Ares is very much the idea of war from the perspective of someone intimately familiar with the world of front line combat and two people desperately trying to kill the other before he kills him first; Athena is a step removed from that, the idea of war more as a concept and ideal, and of trying to outthink your opponent. I think this may apply to her and Hephestus as well. He may be more of an engineer/artisan/maker, while she is more of the idea of invention itself. In my head canon, I think of them both being gods of modern technology (both in the modern day and the past), and not having much conflict over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T10:33:21-08:00","id":1361765,"title":"","content":"(Prometheus)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T11:42:58-08:00","id":1361773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361765#post1361765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Prometheus)</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheus used his powers of Foresight to predict the internet. He's not a Titan related to the Internet, except for one thing.<br /> <br /> You know the primal need to post 'first' on anything with a comment section? He started that. And now it echoes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T12:32:42-08:00","id":1361779,"title":"","content":"Hm Prometheus hiding from Zeus by staying within the internet could make for a nice hook for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T13:03:57-08:00","id":1361783,"title":"","content":"Alternately:<br /> <br /> &quot;So, Prometheus, you escaped my chains and trained liver-eating eagle, but lets see you escape my newest prison: The World Wide Web!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dad! Knock it off! That's not what I invented the Internet for.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But it's a web ....&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not literally!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A net! Just like what your brother used on his wife and brother that time!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's not how this works!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's symbolic! That's all that matters in myths!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fine, whatever.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hahaha, yes, Prometheus, now you will be well and truly googled by the firefoxes of my digital web!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aaaagh!&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T15:53:22-08:00","id":1361800,"title":"","content":"I was referring to Prometheus in the context of the debate between Athena and Hephaestus and the origins of technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T15:59:46-08:00","id":1361801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361800#post1361800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to Prometheus in the context of the debate between Athena and Hephaestus and the origins of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but Prometheus isn't really... Tech-y? Like he gets conflated with fire a lot but really, he doesn't have a lot of metaphorical fire associations. He was the Titan of Foresight, his biggest deed was grabbing fire from Heaven and giving it to people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T18:12:02-08:00","id":1361824,"title":"","content":"And teaching them what it was and how to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T18:38:39-08:00","id":1361830,"title":"","content":"And then he got chained to a rock until Herakles shows up to save him, doing a whole lot of Not-Tech-Related Stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T07:53:47-08:00","id":1361900,"title":"","content":"A different approach to this post. In your opinion, Elon Musk (or a character Musk like) is a Scion of who?...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T09:59:10-08:00","id":1361922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361900#post1361900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A different approach to this post. In your opinion, Elon Musk (or a character Musk like) is a Scion of who?...</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, who's a corrupt figure who represents the worst of capitalism? Musk doesn't know shit about technology and electronics.<br /> <br /> Hell, he didn't even actually found Tesla. He bought it from the actual founders, and part of the purchase contract included giving him rights to call himself the Founderr.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Fomorian, or Mammon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T11:48:26-08:00","id":1361938,"title":"","content":"Hermes, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T14:44:24-08:00","id":1361990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews#post1359863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stated as slight off-topic <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/444750-which-new-pantheons-do-you-want?p=1359842#post1359842&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, we entered in to discussion of how classical Pantheons Gods could take modern Purviews \u2013 for example, Internet. Open topic for lists I will compile once in a while from posts. Only rule \u2013 we propose maximum two gods per Pantheon per concept, so do not having every long lists of things.<br /> <br /> Starting list compiled from my and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> propositions:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Internet</b></span><br /> <br /> Aesir - Heimdall?<br /> Theoi \u2013 Hermes, Iris - she's <i>at least</i> as qualified for the role as Hermes is.<br /> Netjar \u2013 Isis<br /> Devas - Sarasvati, Goddess of Arts and Letters.<br /> Kami - Tsukiyomi - he's big on travel and gossip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's remember Iris and Hermes split the messenger duties. They filled different roles. Similarly they could splits roles to cover the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T14:53:55-08:00","id":1361993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361801#post1361801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but Prometheus isn't really... Tech-y? Like he gets conflated with fire a lot but really, he doesn't have a lot of metaphorical fire associations. He was the Titan of Foresight, his biggest deed was grabbing fire from Heaven and giving it to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Find the book &quot;Gods and Robots&quot; by Adrienne Mayor. Have your mind blown. Hephesaestus was building robots for King Minos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T16:31:29-08:00","id":1362013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361993#post1361993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Find the book &quot;Gods and Robots&quot; by Adrienne Mayor. Have your mind blown. Hephesaestus was building robots for King Minos!</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew about Hephaestus's robotic automatons. That's why I said he'd probably be a God of Tech.<br /> <br /> And why I was saying I couldn't recall offhandedly Prometheus having anything really... Tech-related to him? He showed humans this Fire thing, but like, that's not even because he himself understood Fire innately in any symbolic way. He just swiped it and read humanity the instruction manual.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T20:32:44-08:00","id":1362045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1361922#post1361922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, who's a corrupt figure who represents the worst of capitalism? Musk doesn't know shit about technology and electronics.<br /> <br /> Hell, he didn't even actually found Tesla. He bought it from the actual founders, and part of the purchase contract included giving him rights to call himself the Founderr.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Fomorian, or Mammon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mammon would be the most obvious choice. Or maybe the titan Mara of the Buddhist Pantheon, since I could see the demon of desire embodying the capitalist mindset of hoarding more resources than you could use in a hundred lifetimes and never, ever, finding satisfaction with what you have even if you're living like a god-emperor. There actually aren't that many deities of avarice, now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T02:18:47-08:00","id":1362075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1359863-old-gods-with-modern-purviews?p=1362045#post1362045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mammon would be the most obvious choice. Or maybe the titan Mara of the Buddhist Pantheon, since I could see the demon of desire embodying 